# ============================================================
#  ONLY THING YOU NEED TO EDIT WHEN YOU GET YOUR GEMINI KEY
# ============================================================
# 1. Copy this file to ".env"  (cp .env.example .env)
# 2. Paste your real key below.
# That's it — nothing else in the codebase needs to change.
GEMINI_API_KEY=paste-your-gemini-api-key-here

# Optional — change the Gemini model without touching any code
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Port the backend server runs on
PORT=4000

# Frontend origin allowed to call this backend (CORS + Socket.io)
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# ============================================================
#  Cloudinary — real storage for uploaded documents/photos
# ============================================================
# Free account at https://cloudinary.com -> Dashboard gives you all three
# values below directly (no card required for the free tier).
#
# IMPORTANT: without these, patient document uploads still "work" in the
# UI, but only as a base64 preview saved straight into MongoDB — this is
# what used to silently fail to reach the doctor once a patient attached a
# couple of files, because the whole patient record (photos included) is
# sent as one PATCH request and would blow past the server's body-size
# limit. Filling these in switches uploads to real Cloudinary storage —
# only a small URL is saved on the patient record after that, so this
# stops happening and any file type (PDF, photo, report) opens properly
# for the doctor.
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# ============================================================
#  MongoDB Atlas — patient records + real-time sync
# ============================================================
# Paste your Atlas connection string here (Atlas dashboard -> Connect ->
# "Drivers" -> copy the mongodb+srv:// URI, then put your DB user's real
# password in place of <password>).
#
# IMPORTANT FOR DEMO DAY: if this is left blank, wrong, or Atlas is
# unreachable for any reason, the backend automatically falls back to an
# in-memory store and the ENTIRE app keeps working exactly as before —
# it just won't persist across a server restart. This is intentional so a
# judge on any network, on demo day, can never see a crash because of the
# database. Fill this in when you want real persistence + cross-device
# doctor/patient sync; leave it blank and everything still works.
#
# Common error on some WiFi/VPNs: "Server record does not share hostname
# with parent URI". This is a DNS issue with mongodb+srv:// links, not a
# bug — try a different network, or in Atlas use Database -> Connect ->
# Drivers -> the legacy "Node.js 2.2.12 or earlier" option to get a
# standard mongodb://host1,host2,host3/... string instead, and paste that
# here. Full guidance also prints in the terminal if this happens.
MONGODB_URI=
